#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Describes an origin server."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/name/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/name/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/name/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Name of an origin. It must be unique within this property.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/servers/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/servers/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/servers/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Each entry should be a string consisting of an address optionally followed "
"by one or more parameters, separated by space characters. The address can "
"take one of the following three forms:\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>{hostname or IP address}</li>\n"
"<li>{hostname or IP address}:{HTTP port}</li>\n"
"<li>{hostname or IP address}:{HTTP port},{HTTPS port}</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"\n"
"The IP address can be either IPv4 or IPv6.  IPv6 is supported if the "
"property's <i>enableIpv6Origin</i> setting is <i>true</i>.  IPv6 addresses "
"can be specified in uncompressed or compressed format, for example, "
"<code>2001:1234:0000:0000:1b12:0000:0000:1a13</code> or "
"<code>2001:1234::1b12:0:0:1a13</code>.\n"
"\n"
"Values for the HTTP and HTTPS ports should be integers in the range "
"[1,65535]. \n"
"Even if the value of <i>supportedProtocol</i> is \"https\", the HTTPS port "
"must be specified after the comma.\n"
"In the third form, one of the two ports can be empty.\n"
"\n"
"If specifying an IPv6 address along with a port, the IPv6 address should be "
"enclosed in brackets, for example, "
"<code>[2001:0DB7:AC10:FE01:0000:0000:0000:0000]:8080</code>\n"
"\n"
"Supported parameters are \"backup\" and \"weight\".\n"
"\n"
"\"backup\" is used to indicate the server is a backup server. It will be "
"used when the primary servers are unavailable.\n"
"\n"
"\"weight\" is a value in the range [1, 100]. The default value is 1. It lets "
"you control the likelihood that one origin server will be used relative to "
"another.\n"
"\n"
"There should be at least one primary server defined; it does not have the "
"\"backup\" parameter.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"<code>[\"www.abc.com weight=1\", \"www1.abc.com:8080 weight=4\", "
"\"www2.abc.com:880,4443 backup\"]</code>\n"
"\n"
"This example specifies two primary servers which are used in a 1:4 ratio "
"meaning one gets about 20% of the requests to origin while the other gets "
"80% of the requests. In addition, a backup server is specified.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/supportedProtocol/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/supportedProtocol/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/supportedProtocol/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This optional field indicates the protocol supported by the origin server. "
"If this property has a certificate attached to it, the value can be set to "
"<i>http</i> if the <i>allowProtocolDowngrade</i> field is also set to "
"<i>true</i>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/verifyOrigin/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/verifyOrigin/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/verifyOrigin/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Optional. It controls whether the cache will validate the certificate of the "
"origin."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/hostHeader/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/hostHeader/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/hostHeader/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Optional. It should be a valid hostname. It will also be used as the SNI "
"servername when contacting the HTTPS origin. We also allow it to be an nginx "
"variable that begins with ‘$’ followed by [a-z_]{3,60}. Nginx variable names "
"are case insensitive, so we only allow lowercase characters.\n"
"If not specified, the value of the HOST header in the request will be "
"used. \n"
"\n"
"One constraint is that if \"awsS3\" is specified for origin authentication, "
"the value of <i>hostHeader</i> cannot be a variable or empty. It has to be a "
"valid Amazon S3 or S3-compatible hostname. Refer to https://"
"docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/VirtualHosting.html"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/directConnection/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/directConnection/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/directConnection/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Optional. This parameter tells us how important it is to directly go to this "
"origin without going through any intermediate cache to fetch content. The "
"values can be \"noDirect\", \"auto\", \"alwaysDirect\".\n"
"\n"
"\"noDirect\" means we always go through at least one intermediate cache. "
"Customers who care particularly about the origin's workload can use this "
"option. Our cache scheduler will dynamically pick the intermediate cache "
"based on performance and resource availability.\n"
"\n"
"\"auto\" means the cache scheduler will make the choice dynamically based on "
"performance and resource availability. This is the default behavior if not "
"specified.\n"
"\n"
"\"alwaysDirect\" means we always directly connect to this origin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/shield/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/shield/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/shield/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Refers to the ID of an origin shield representing a set of servers that will "
"make requests to your origin servers rather than the CDN Pro edge servers. "
"This can help further reduce traffic to your origin. This is an advanced "
"feature that can be enabled by contacting our support team. The <a "
"href=\"#operation/get-cdn-shields\">origin shields API</a> provides a list "
"of available shields along with their IP addresses. It is best if you select "
"a shield whose region is closest to your origin servers. Use of a shield in "
"China requires your property have 'hasBeian' set to <i>true</i>. If your "
"origin servers have an access control list, add the IPs of the shield you "
"choose to use."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/keepAliveTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/keepAliveTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/keepAliveTimeout/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Timeout in seconds during which an idle keepalive connection to an upstream "
"server will stay open. A service quota setting of "
"<i>maxUpstreamKeepaliveTimeOut</i> can change the maximum permitted value."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to specify the number of unsuccessful attempts to "
"reach one of the origin's IP addresses or peers before it is marked as "
"<i>unavailable</i> for a period of time designated by the timeout. The "
"number of attempts should be specified in a subfield of the "
"peerFailureTimeout object called <i>failureThreshold</i> while the timeout "
"in seconds should be in a subfield called <i>timeout</i>. If all peers of "
"all servers are unavailable, requests for content from the origin will "
"receive an immediate 502 HTTP response. By default, six attempts to a peer "
"are made, after which a one-second timeout applies to that peer. To disable "
"this feature, set peerFailureTimeout to \"<i>off</i>\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/failureThreshold/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/failureThreshold/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/failureThreshold/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Number of attempts to connect to a peer before it is considered unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/timeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/timeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerFailureTimeout/properties/timeout/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Timeout in seconds."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/peerSelectionAlgorithm/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerSelectionAlgorithm/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/peerSelectionAlgorithm/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This setting controls how the origin server is selected when an origin "
"server's hostname resolves to multiple IP addresses. "
"<table><tr><td>round_robin</td><td> Rotate among the peers sequentially. "
"This is the default setting, which tries to evenly distribute the origin "
"traffic to all the peers.</td></tr><tr><td>consistent_hash</"
"td><td>Distribute the origin traffic based on the hash value of the URL. If "
"the origin server has a cache, this option should help with the hit ratio.</"
"td></tr><tr><td>sorted_list</td><td>Select the peer based on the network "
"quality. When the origin peers are geographically distributed (such as "
"another CDN), this option should help ensure consistent performance.</td></"
"tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/maxConnections/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/maxConnections/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/maxConnections/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Defines the maximum number of simultaneous connections to the origin. The "
"default is '0', which indicates connections are unlimited."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Refers to a <a href=\"#tag/Certificate-Management\">certificate</a> used to "
"authenticate with the origin server. This certificate must also be deployed."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Optional. It is a structure to specify the parameters, such as password, for "
"authentication with the origin servers. It should have at least one field: "
"\"methodName\", which should be a string indicating one of the predefined "
"authentication methods. The only valid value at this time is \"awsS3\". When "
"\"awsS3\" is used, the following parameters are required:\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>awsS3.region</li>\n"
"<li>awsS3.accessKey</li>\n"
"<li>awsS3.secretKey</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"\n"
"The value specified for \"awsS3.secretKey\" must not be plain text secret "
"key. Instead, create a \"secret\" object, and then use the "
"`$SECRET(secret.name)` syntax here to refer to the secret containing the "
"secret key. This avoids exposure of the sensitive information.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"<code>\n"
"{\"methodName\":\"awsS3\",\n"
"\"awsS3\":{\n"
"\"region\":\"us-west-1\",\n"
"\"accessKey\":\"sdnu2932\",\n"
"\"secretKey\":\"$SECRET(mysecret)\"\n"
"}}\n"
"</code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/properties/methodName/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/properties/methodName/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/origins/items/properties/authentication/properties/methodName/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Authentication method."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/allowProtocolDowngrade/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowProtocolDowngrade/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowProtocolDowngrade/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This setting applies only if the property has an attached certificate "
"allowing client requests to use HTTPS. If the value of "
"allowProtocolDowngrade is <i>false</i>, we require all the origin servers to "
"support HTTPS. If the value is <i>true</i>, we allow origins that support "
"only HTTP, which reduces security.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/enableIpv6Origin/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableIpv6Origin/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableIpv6Origin/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Enable use of IPv6 addresses to access the property's origin servers."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/followClientIpVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/followClientIpVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/followClientIpVersion/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"When enableIpv6Origin is enabled, this setting controls whether to match the "
"addressing method used by a client if a request to the origin is required to "
"fetch content. <table><tr><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th></tr><tr><td>auto</"
"td><td>Attempt to reach the origin server using the same IP addressing as "
"the client, but use the other version as backup if needed.</td></"
"tr><tr><td>strict</td><td>Use only the same addressing method as the client "
"when accessing the origin for content.</td></tr><tr><td>off</td><td>Use both "
"IPv4 and IPv6 addressing to reach the origin, regardless of the IP "
"addressing method used by the client.</td></tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/edgeLogic/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/edgeLogic/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/edgeLogic/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Refer to the [Edge Logic Introduction](</docs/edge-logic/intro>) to learn "
"how to use the NGINX language to further customize CDN Pro to meet your "
"business requirements."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/syntaxVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/syntaxVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/syntaxVersion/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "The value must be set to 1 at this time."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/cacheKeyHostname/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/cacheKeyHostname/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/cacheKeyHostname/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"The cachekey hostname must be a string made of lowercase letters, digits, "
"dot, dash, and underscore. If not specified, the incoming Host header value "
"will be used and the cache will not be shared across different hostnames in "
"this property.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/cacheKeyUri/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/cacheKeyUri/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/cacheKeyUri/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This setting controls how the URI of the incoming request is incorporated "
"into the cache key if you use a \"rewrite\" directive in the property's Edge "
"Logic. The default value, \"preRewrite\", puts the unmodified URI into the "
"cache key while \"postRewrite\" uses the modified URI. If your rewrite "
"directive converts multiple different URIs into the same value, using "
"\"postRewrite\" may result in a higher cache hit ratio."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/schemeInCacheKey/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/schemeInCacheKey/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/schemeInCacheKey/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the scheme (\"http\" or \"https\") should be included in "
"the cache key. Default behavior is </i>false</i>. Set to <i>true</i> if the "
"content is known to be different for different schemes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/redirectHttpToHttps/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/redirectHttpToHttps/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/redirectHttpToHttps/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This field can be set to either a boolean value or a string. If the value is "
"set to <i>true</i>, the server will redirect all HTTP requests to HTTPS "
"using status code 301. You can also specify string values \"302\", \"307\", "
"or \"308\" instead if you wish to return a different status code when a "
"request is redirected."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/disableHttp2/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/disableHttp2/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/disableHttp2/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Set to <i>true</i> to disable support for HTTP/2 and support only HTTP 1.1. "
"HTTP/2 requires TLS to work, so you must specify a certificate in the "
"tlsCertificateId field to support HTTP/2."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/enableHttp3/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableHttp3/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableHttp3/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Set to <i>true</i> to enable support for HTTP/3. HTTP/3 requires TLS to "
"work, so this field will be ignored unless you specify a certificate in the "
"tlsCertificateId field."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/extraServicePorts/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This field lists ports other than the default 80 used to handle HTTP "
"requests and ports other than the default 443 used to handle HTTPS requests. "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/http/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/http/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/http/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This is a list of ports other than 80 which are used to handle HTTP "
"requests. The available values can be found in the <a href=\"#operation/get-"
"cdn-systemConfigs\">systemConfigs</a> API's response. If you need another "
"port, please contact our support team."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/https/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/https/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/https/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This is a list of ports other than 443 which are used to handle HTTPS "
"requests. The available values can be found in the <a href=\"#operation/get-"
"cdn-systemConfigs\">systemConfigs</a> API's response. If you need another "
"port, please contact our support team."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCertificateId/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Refers to a <a href=\"#tag/Certificate-Management\">certificate</a>. Specify "
"a certificate to enable HTTPS for the hostnames of this property. It can be "
"of type RSA or EC."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsCertificateId1/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCertificateId1/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCertificateId1/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Refers to a <a href=\"#tag/Certificate-Management\">certificate</a>. "
"Optionally specify a second certificate to be used for HTTPS for the "
"hostnames of this property. It must be of a different type (RSA or EC) than "
"the certificate specified in <i>tlsCertificateId</i>. When there are two "
"certificates available for your hostnames, the client and server will "
"negotiate at the time of requests to pick one of the certificates for SSL. "
"This could mean better performance and fault tolerance.  It is invalid to "
"set only the <i>tlsCertificateId1</i> field without setting the "
"<i>tlsCertificateId</i> field.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsMinVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsMinVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsMinVersion/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Minimum required TLS version. TLS versions 1.0 and 1.1 have been deprecated "
"for security reasons, so we strongly recommend a minimum of TLS 1.2."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsMaxVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsMaxVersion/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsMaxVersion/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum supported TLS version. TLS versions 1.0 and 1.1 have been deprecated "
"for security reasons, so we strongly recommend a minimum of TLS 1.2."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsCiphers/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCiphers/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsCiphers/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Any cipher list supported by \"openssl ciphers\". See https://"
"www.openssl.org/docs/manmaster/man1/ciphers.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/enableOcspStapling/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableOcspStapling/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/enableOcspStapling/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Enables <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCSP_stapling\">Online "
"Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) stapling</a> to check the revocation "
"status of digital certificates. No OCSP response will be stapled to TLS "
"handshakes if there is no OCSP URL specified on your certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tls0Rtt/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tls0Rtt/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tls0Rtt/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Enable TLS zero round-trip time, a feature of TLS 1.3 that can improve "
"performance for repeat visits to a site. If enabling it though, be sure your "
"site is not vulnerable to the HTTP replay attack."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsSessionTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsSessionTimeout/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsSessionTimeout/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Lifespan of TLS session ticket in seconds."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsVerifyClient/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsVerifyClient/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsVerifyClient/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Whether to enable verification of a client's certificate. "
"<table><tr><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th></tr><tr><td>on</td><td>verify the "
"client certificate</td></tr><tr><td>off</td><td>do not verify the client "
"certificate</td></tr><tr><td>optional</td><td>request the client certificate "
"and verify it if it is present</td></tr><tr><td>noCA</td><td>request the "
"client certificate but do not require it to be signed by a trusted CA "
"certificate</td></tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/tlsClientCACertId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsClientCACertId/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/tlsClientCACertId/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"ID of a CA certificate. This field is required if tlsVerifyClient is <i>on</"
"i> or <i>optional</i>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/disableCertAutomation/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/disableCertAutomation/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/disableCertAutomation/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"By default, CDN Pro takes control of the contents under the /.well-known/"
"{acme-challenge, pki-validation} directories to support certificate auto-"
"renew for properties. If for any reason you need to manage these two "
"directories by yourself on the origin, for example, to implement your own "
"certificate auto-renew mechanism, you can use this configuration option to "
"disable the default behavior by setting its value to <i>true</i>. For more "
"information about our support for certificate auto-renewal, refer to the "
"description of the <i>autoRenew</i> field in the <a href=\"#operation/"
"createCertificate\">Create a certificate API</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Specify one or more access control rules to restrict access to your content. "
"More advanced configuration can be done using Edge Logic. These access "
"control rules take precedence over Edge Logic if both are defined."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/title
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/title
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/title
#. (+1 more)
msgid "accessControlRule"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"This object defines a rule that can be used to restrict access to your "
"content. More complex rules can be created using CDN Pro's Edge Logic."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/id/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/id/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/id/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "An optional ID for the access control rule."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Specify the conditions that the incoming request must match. At least one "
"condition must be specified. If multiple are specified, all must match."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/scheme/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/scheme/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/scheme/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "Indicates whether the incoming request uses HTTP or HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/hostname/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/hostname/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/hostname/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Indicates the hostname requested. It must be one of the hostnames defined in "
"the property. If a wildcard hostname is configured in the property, you can "
"specify either the wildcard hostname or a specific hostname matching the "
"wildcard. For example, if the wildcard was \"*.xyz.com\", then you could "
"enter a hostname such as \"w.xyz.com\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/uri/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions~1{version}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/uri/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1properties~1{propertyID}~1versions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accessControlRules/items/properties/conditions/properties/uri/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid "The URI begins with \"/\" and can end with \"*\" for prefix matching. "
msgstr ""

