"always be <i>false</i> for a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/get/description
msgid ""
"Gets details about a certificate including the versions of the certificate "
"and who is using it."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/summary
msgid "Update a certificate"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"A new certificate version was successfully created. The Location header will "
"be a URL to the new certificate version. Example:  <code>Location: https://"
"ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/cdn/certificates/329f12c1fe6708c23c31e91f/versions/5</"
"code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL to the new certificate version. The URL follows this format: https://"
"ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/cdn/certificates/{certificateId}/versions/{version} "
"where {certificateId} represents the ID of the certificate and {version} "
"represents the new certificate version. If you would like to get the "
"certificate version, simply extract the last portion of the path and ignore "
"the rest. "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/responses/400/description
msgid ""
"This response indicates the request was invalid. Please refer to the "
"response body for more details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/responses/403/description
msgid ""
"The request was forbidden. Please refer to the response body for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/description
msgid ""
"Update a certificate using this API. The fields are the same as those in the "
"<a href=\"#operation/createCertificate\">Create a certificate API</a>. If "
"the certificate is currently used by properties deployed to production or "
"staging, we recommend that you follow this API call by <a href=\"#operation/"
"createDeployment\">creating a deployment task</a> to deploy the updated "
"certificate. Otherwise, CDN Pro may still serve content using an older "
"version of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/description/description
msgid "Description of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/sharingMethod/description
msgid ""
"This field can be used only by resellers to indicate who can use the "
"certificate. \"All\" indicates all child customers can use the certificate; "
"\"none\" indicates no child customers can use it. If the value is \"some\", "
"specify the child customers allowed to use the certificate in the "
"<i>shareWith</i> field."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/shareWith/description
msgid ""
"If you are a reseller choosing to share the certificate with \"some\" "
"customers, this field indicates the IDs of the customers who can use it."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/autoRenew/description
msgid ""
"Indicates whether the certificate will be renewed with Let's Encrypt. The "
"value must remain <i>Off</i> for CA certificates."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/newVersion/description
msgid ""
"If this field is present, a new version of the certificate will be created. "
"If the <i>identificationInfo</i> field is not provided, then the information "
"will be copied from the latest version of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/newVersion/properties/privateKey/description
msgid ""
"If not present, the value will be copied from the latest version of the "
"certificate. Please refer to the description of the <i>privateKey</i> field "
"in the <a href=\"#operation/createCertificate\">Create a certificate API</a> "
"for details about the format. This field should not be specified for CA "
"certificates."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/newVersion/properties/certificate/description
msgid ""
"If not present, the value will be copied from the latest version of the "
"certificate. Please refer to the description of the <i>certificate</i> field "
"in the <a href=\"#operation/createCertificate\">Create a certificate API</a> "
"for details about the format. This field should not be specified for CA "
"certificates."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/newVersion/properties/chainCert/description
msgid ""
"This field must be filled in if the <i>privateKey</i> and <i>certificate</i> "
"fields are both omitted. If you are creating a new version of a CA "
"certificate, you must specify this field. In this case, only the chain "
"certificate will be updated. The chain certificate must be in PEM format."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/forceRenew/description
msgid ""
"A value of <i>true</i> requests the certificate to be auto-renewed as soon "
"as possible instead of waiting for the certificate to expire in 15 days. The "
"value will be set to false after a successful renewal. The value must remain "
"<i>false</i> for CA certificates."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/patch/requestBody/description
msgid ""
"The request body indicates the fields that will be updated. If a field is "
"omitted, then its value will be unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/delete/summary
msgid "Delete a certificate"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/delete/responses/204/description
msgid "This response is returned if the certificate was successfully deleted."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/delete/responses/404/description
msgid "The certificate was not found."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/delete/responses/409/description
msgid ""
"The certificate cannot be deleted because it is being used in production or "
"staging."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}/delete/description
msgid ""
"This API lets you delete a certificate that is not being used in production "
"or staging."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/summary
msgid "Download the CSR"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/description
msgid ""
"Obtain the certificate signing request (CSR) information. You can take it to "
"a certificate authority to apply for a certificate. Once you have it, you "
"should update our system using the <a href=\"#operation/"
"updateCertificate\">Update a certificate API</a>. This API cannot be used "
"for CA certificates."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/description
msgid "The response contains the CSR."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/csr/description
msgid "The CSR."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/latestVersion/description
msgid "Most recent version of the certifiate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/ownerCustomerId/description
msgid "A reference to the customer that owns the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dcvFile/description
msgid ""
"This field is only returned if the <i>dcv</i> query parameter is specified."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dcvFile/properties/uri/description
msgid ""
"A URI that is accessible on your hostnames using the certificate. The file's "
"content will consist of a SHA-256 hash and the domain sectigo.com. Example:\n"
"\n"
"<pre>\n"
"a6e96b23f9e2add3f79c2907ded1adc43961b05f6d702758a200a8ec8b4d7115\n"
"sectigo.com\n"
"</pre>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dcvFile/properties/expirationTime/description
msgid "An RFC 3339 date indicating when the file expires."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1csr/get/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"This optional parameter can be used to request a domain control validation "
"(DCV) file. Currently, we support the certificate authority, Sectigo, by "
"specifying \"sectigo\" as the value of the parameter."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/parameters/0/description
msgid ""
"Version of the certificate. It can be an integer representing the version "
"like \"2\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/parameters/1/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1latest/parameters/0/description
msgid "ID of a certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/summary
msgid "Get a certificate version's details"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/description
msgid "The response contains details about the version of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/version/description
msgid "The certificate version."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/comments/description
msgid "Comments about the certificate version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/expirationTime/description
msgid ""
"An RFC3339 format date indicating when the certificate version expires. This "
"field will be returned only for a server certificate not a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/creationTime/description
msgid ""
"An RFC 3339 format date indicating when the certificate version was created."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/subject/description
msgid ""
"The certificate subject. This field will be returned only for a server "
"certificate not a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/signatureAlgo/description
msgid ""
"The signature algorithm used by the certificate. This field will be returned "
"only for a server certificate not a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/serialNumber/description
msgid ""
"The serial number associated with the certificate. This field will be "
"returned only for a server certificate not a CA certificate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/inProduction/description
msgid ""
"Indicates whether the certificate version is currently deployed to "
"production."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/inStaging/description
msgid ""
"Indicates whether the certificate version is currently deployed to staging.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/fingerprint/description
msgid ""
"certificate fingerprint. This field will be returned only for a server "
"certificate not a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/algorithm/description
msgid ""
"The encryption algorithm. This field will be returned only for a server "
"certificate not a CA certificate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/keyLength/description
msgid ""
"Number of bits used in encryption. This field will be returned only for a "
"server certificate not a CA certificate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/subjectAlternativeNames/description
msgid ""
"List of hostnames served by the certificate. Wildcards are permitted, for "
"example, *.domain.com. This field will be returned only for a server "
"certificate not a CA certificate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/chainCertificates/description
msgid "Describes the certificate chain."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/chainCertificates/items/properties/subject/description
msgid "Subject of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/chainCertificates/items/properties/expirationTime/description
msgid "RFC 3339 format date indicating when the certificate expires."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/chainCertificates/items/properties/signatureAlgo/description
msgid "Algorithm of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/chainCertificates/items/properties/issuer/description
msgid "Issuer of the chain certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/issuer/description
msgid ""
"Issuer of the certificate. This field will be returned only for a server "
"certificate not a CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/type/description
msgid ""
"Indicates the type of certificate, either \"uploaded\" or \"self-signed.\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/deletable/description
msgid ""
"Whether or not the certificate version can be deleted. A version can be "
"deleted if it is not the only version, and it has never been deployed to "
"staging or production."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/get/description
msgid ""
"Obtain details about a certificate version including the expiration date, "
"algorithm and key length, fingerprint, and whether it is deployed in "
"production and staging."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/delete/summary
msgid "Delete the latest version of a certificate"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/delete/responses/204/description
msgid "The certificate version was deleted."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/delete/responses/404/description
msgid "Invalid certificate. Refer to the response body for details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/delete/responses/409/description
msgid ""
"The certificate version could not be deleted. Refer to the response body for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1certificates~1{certificateID}~1versions~1{version}/delete/description
msgid ""
"This endpoint can be used to delete the latest version of a certificate if "
"it was never deployed before. The version number will be reused the next "
"time the certificate is <a href=\"#operation/updateCertificate\">updated to "
"a new version</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/summary
msgid "Get list of property validation tasks"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/description
msgid "A list of validation tasks"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/count/description
msgid "Total number of validation tasks"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/description
msgid ""
"Summarizes validation tasks. Further details about a validation task can be "
"obtained by calling the <a href=\"#operation/queryValidationTask\">Query a "
"property validation task API</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/id/description
msgid "ID of the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/propertyId/description
msgid "ID of the property that was validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/version/description
msgid "Version of the property that was validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/submissionTime/description
msgid ""
"An RFC 3339 format string indicating when the validation task was submitted. "
"Example: \"2019-11-12T03:09:26Z\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/status/description
msgid "Status of the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/cacheVersion/description
msgid ""
"Identifies the internal cache version on which the property was validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/apiRequestId/description
msgid "Indicates the associated API request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/apiAccountId/description
msgid "An API account that generated the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/customerId/description
msgid ""
"ID of the customer who owns the property will be returned to a reseller "
"using the Report-Range header with a value of self+children or children-only."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/validations/items/properties/finishTime/description
msgid ""
"An RFC 3339 format string indicating when the validation task finished. "
"Example: \"2024-11-12T03:09:26Z\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/responses/400/description
msgid "The request was invalid. Refer to the response body for more details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/description
msgid ""
"Get a list of property validation tasks including the associated property "
"ID, version, submission time, and status. Filter the results using the query "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/0/description
msgid "Return validation tasks associated only with a specific property ID."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/1/description
msgid "Return validation tasks only for a particular property version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/2/description
msgid "Indicates the maximum number of validation tasks to return."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/3/description
msgid "Indicates the index of the first validation task to return."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/4/description
msgid ""
"The results will be filtered based on the presence of the value as a "
"validation task ID or in a task name."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/5/description
msgid ""
"Return results sorted by when the task was submitted (submissionTime) or "
"when the task was completed (finishTime). "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/6/description
msgid "Return results sorted in ascending (asc) or descending (desc) order.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/8/description
msgid ""
"Enter an RFC 3339 format date to return validation tasks which were "
"submitted by this date."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/9/description
msgid ""
"Enter an RFC 3339 format date to return validation tasks which were "
"submitted no later than this date."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/10/description
msgid ""
"An optional header that resellers can use to specify whether to include data "
"from children customers. <table><tr><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th></"
"tr><tr><td>self-only</td><td>Include validation tasks of the caller.</td></"
"tr><tr><td>children-only</td><td>Include validation tasks of children "
"customers only.</td></tr><tr><td>self+children</td><td>Include validation "
"tasks of both the caller and children customers.</td></tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/get/parameters/11/description
msgid ""
"Filter based on the task's status. By default, tasks are returned regardless "
"of their status."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/summary
msgid "Create a validation task"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"A validation task was successfully created. A Location header containing the "
"URL of the new validation task is returned. Example: <code>Location: https://"
"ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/cdn/validations/5dca2205f9e9cc0001df7b24</code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL allowing you to get details about the new validation task.  The URL "
"follows this format: https://ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/cdn/validations/{taskId} "
"where {taskId} represents the ID of the newly created validation task. If "
"you would like to get the task ID, simply extract the last portion of the "
"path and ignore the rest."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/responses/400/description
msgid ""
"The validation task could not be created. Refer to the response body for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/description
msgid ""
"This API validates a property version. You must call this API before you can "
"<a href=\"#operation/createDeployment\">deploy the property version</a> to "
"staging or production. Your property will be checked for correct syntax."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/name/description
msgid "Name of the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/propertyId/description
msgid "Indicates the property to validate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/version/description
msgid "Indicates the version of the property to validate."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/webhook/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/webhook/description
msgid "ID of a webhook to call when the validation task completes."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/parameters/0/description
msgid "ID of a validation task"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/summary
msgid "Get property validation task"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/description
msgid ""
"Refer to the response body for details about the validation task. It may "
"have succeeded or failed or be in progress, or still being queued to run."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/propertyId/description
msgid "ID of the property being validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/version/description
msgid "Version of the property being validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/submissionTime/description
msgid ""
"An RFC 3339 format string indicating when the task was created. Example: "
"\"2019-11-12T03:06:16Z\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/status/description
msgid "Indicates the validation task's status."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/statusDetails/description
msgid "Further information about the task's current status.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customerId/description
msgid "ID of the customer whose property is validated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiRequestId/description
msgid "Refers to the ID of the associated API request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/finishTime/description
msgid "An RFC 3339 date indicating when the task finished."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/name/description
msgid "Name of the property validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiAccountId/description
msgid "ID of an API account used to create the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiName/description
msgid "Name of an API account used to create the validation task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1validations~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/cacheVersion/description
