#. /paths/~1cdn~1deploymentTasks/post/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"If you deploy a property using a server certificate, we check that the "
"hostnames in the property are covered by the subject alternative name (SAN) "
"of the certificate and that the certificate has not expired. For test "
"purposes, you can bypass this check by passing the <i>Check-Certificate: no</"
"i> header when creating the deployment task. You should not use this header "
"when deploying for real users of your content since their browsers will warn "
"about the invalid certificate and discourage them from visiting."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1deploymentTasks/post/parameters/2/description
msgid ""
"If you deploy a property using a certificate for origin authentication, we "
"check that the certificate has not expired. For test purposes, you can "
"bypass this check by passing the <i>Check-Origin-Auth-Certificate: no</i> "
"header when creating the deployment task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1deploymentTasks/post/parameters/3/description
msgid ""
"If you deploy a property using a CA certificate for client verification, we "
"check that the certificate has not expired. For test purposes, you can "
"bypass this check by passing the <i>Check-Client-CA-Certificate: no</i> "
"header when creating the deployment task."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1deploymentTasks/post/parameters/4/description
msgid ""
"By default, we check if the deployment would result in removal of hostnames "
"which have been recently used as determined by the number of requests to "
"them in the past 24 hours. If this is the case, the API returns an error "
"with the code 'RemovingActiveHostname'. This safety check is intended to "
"protect against accidentally impacting visitors to your content.  You can "
"pass the <i>Check-Usage: no</i> header to bypass this check."
msgstr ""

