"properties will be returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1vol/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/propertyHostnames/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1vol/post/requestBody/content/application~1xml/schema/properties/filters/properties/propertyHostnames/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1volOrigin/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/propertyHostnames/description
#. (+17 more)
msgid ""
"A list of property hostnames for which to return data. These correspond to "
"values in the <i>hostnames</i> field of a property configuration. These can "
"differ from the value sent in an HTTP request. For example, if you <a "
"href=\"#operation/createProperty\">create a property</a> to accelerate "
"'*.test.com', a client could request content and pass a Host header of "
"'abc.test.com'. In this case, '\\*.test.com' is a property hostname you can "
"filter by using this field while 'abc.test.com' is a hostname you can filter "
"by using the hostnames field. By default, data for all property hostnames is "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1vol/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/legacyTypes/description
