msgid ""
"Create a purge request to force a refresh of the content stored in the CDN "
"Pro cache servers.  You may wish to do this if you just updated content on "
"your origin server and want visitors to see the changes right away rather "
"than wait for the updates to propagate according to the schedule defined in "
"your property configuration."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/name/description
msgid "A description of the purge request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/fileUrls/description
msgid ""
"URLs of files to purge.  File URLs should not contain the asterisk "
"character, '*'.   If a directory or filename in a URL includes a percent "
"character, '%', be sure to encode it. A URL can be up to 2048 characters."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/fileHeaders/description
msgid ""
"If a file's cache key depends on request headers, you can specify the header "
"values that are applicable to purge one version of the cached file. The same "
"set of header values will apply to all entries in <i>fileUrls</i>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/fileHeaders/items/properties/name/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/fileHeaders/items/properties/name/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirHeaders/items/properties/name/description
#. (+2 more)
msgid "HTTP header name."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirUrls/description
msgid ""
"URLs to purge. URLs must begin with <i>http://</i> or <i>https://</i> and "
"can be up to 2048 characters. Use the '\\*' character to purge multiple "
"files or directories. If a URL has multiple sets of asterisk characters, "
"only the last '\\*' or '\\*\\*' will be treated as a wildcard. Other "
"instances of '\\*' earlier in the URL will be treated as the literal "
"character '*'.\n"
"<table><tr><th>Example</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir</td><td>Purge all variations of a "
"single directory, but not its subdirectories or files. Variations may exist "
"if custom cache keys are used.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/**</td><td>Purge all files and "
"subdirectories whose cache key begins with <i>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/"
"</i>.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/*</td><td>Purge all files, but not "
"subdirectories, within a directory.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/*.jpg</td><td>Purge all cache entries "
"ending with the .jpg file extension. Subdirectories of http://"
"test.domain2.com/mydir/ are not purged. </td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/a*</td><td>Purge all files, but not "
"subdirectories, that start with the letter 'a'.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/a**</td><td>Purge all files and "
"subdirectories that start with the letter 'a'.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/mydir/a.jpg</td><td>Purge all variations of "
"\"a.jpg\". Variations may exist if custom cache keys are used.</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>http://test.domain2.com/my**jpg</td><td>Purge all entries whose "
"cache key begins with <i>http://test.domain2.com/my</i> and ends with the "
"suffix <i>jpg</i>. The \"**\" can match anything in the path including "
"additional subdirectories. For example, http://test.domain2.com/mydirectory/"
"picture.jpg would be purged.</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
"If a directory or filename in a URL includes a percent character, '%', be "
"sure to encode it."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/action/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/action/description
msgid ""
"This controls whether cached files and directories should be removed "
"altogether from the CDN Pro servers (delete) or flagged as invalid "
"(invalidate)."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/target/description
msgid ""
"Specify if the purge request applies to the staging or production "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/webhook/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/webhook/description
msgid "ID of a webhook to call when the purge task completes."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/regexPatterns/description
msgid ""
"Regular expression patterns used to match the cache key. Each must begin "
"with the following format: \n"
" <i>{scheme}://{hostname}/</i>. {scheme} can be <i>http</i>, <i>https</i>, "
"or <i>any</i>, which matches any scheme.\n"
"Example: \n"
"<code>https://test.domain.com/my.*\\.(jpg|png)\\?q=</code>\n"
"<br/>\n"
"For performance considerations, the following restrictions apply:\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>The regular expression pattern following the hostname can be up to 126 "
"characters.\n"
"</li>\n"
"<li>It can consist of up to two unlimited quantifiers (\"*\", \"+\", or \",}"
"\").</li>\n"
"<li>The upper limit on a quantifier cannot be more than 59, for example, "
"<code>{1,59}</code></li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1purges/post/requestBody/description
msgid ""
"The request body is used to specify the files and directories to purge, the "
