#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/isMaster/description
#. (+1 more)
msgid ""
"Indicates whether this portal user has full access to all subscribed "
"products."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/products/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/products/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/products/description
msgid ""
"List of products that the user has access to. The default is no products. "
"You can specify \"CDN\" to represent CDN Pro, and \"HDT\" for High-Speed "
"Data Transmission. This field is ignored for master contacts, as a master "
"contact has access to all subscribed products."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/canImpersonate/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/canImpersonate/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/canImpersonate/description
msgid ""
"This setting applies to resellers only. It indicates whether the user can "
"impersonate child customers. A value of \"all\" means the user can "
"impersonate all child customers. A value of \"none\" means the user cannot "
"impersonate any. This field works with the <i>impersonateExceptions</i> "
"field."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/status/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/status/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/status/description
msgid ""
"Indicates the status of the portal user account. An 'active' user has full "
"access to the portal. A 'suspended' user cannot log in.  A 'pending' user is "
"one that has been invited to use the portal but has not completed setting up "
"the account.  You cannot call the <a href=\"#operation/"
"createContact\">Create a  portal user</a> or <a href=\"#operation/patch-"
"ngadmin-contacts-id\">Update a portal user</a> APIs with a status value of "
"'pending'."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/impersonateExceptions/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/impersonateExceptions/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/impersonateExceptions/description
msgid ""
"This setting applies to resellers only.  It contains a list of customer IDs "
"that are exceptions to the rule defined by the <i>canImpersonate</i> field. "
"For example, if <i>canImpersonate</i> is \"all\" the portal user can "
"impersonate all child customers of the reseller. Entering one or more "
"customer IDs as exceptions will prevent the user from impersonating those "
"particular child customers. Conversely, if <i>canImpersonate</i> is "
"\"none\", entries in the exception list represent customers who can be "
"impersonated by this user."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/ipWhiteList/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/ipWhiteList/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1contacts~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/properties/ipWhiteList/description
msgid ""
"List of IP addresses from which the portal user can log in. This list "
"applies in addition to the portalSettings.ipWhiteList's addresses you can <a "
"href=\"#operation/patch-ngadmin-customers-id\">set up at the customer level."
"</a> You can specify a range, an individual IP address, or an IP in CIDR "
"notation. Compressed and uncompressed IPv6 addresses are also permitted. "
"Example: <code>[\\\"1.1.1.1-1.1.1.8\\\", \\\"1.2.3.4\\\", \\\"1.5.5.0/24\\"
"\"]</code>"
msgstr ""

