#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/summary
msgid "Update a customer"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/responses/200/description
msgid ""
"The customer account was updated successfully. The response body will "
"contain the current settings."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/responses/403/description
msgid "The API call was forbidden. Refer to the response body for details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/description
msgid ""
"Update a customer account. Settings within the <i>configs</i> field can only "
"be set by a reseller on behalf of a child customer. A child customer's "
"access to a product can only be removed if they are not currently using "
"resources. For example, the child should not have any remaining deployed "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiKey/description
msgid ""
"If specified, the value must be \"reset\". A new key will be generated for "
"the administrator API account and must be used for all future API calls "
"using that account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/ipWhiteList/description
msgid ""
"List of IP addresses from which API calls using API accounts are permitted. "
"This list works with each <a href=\"#operation/post-ngadmin-"
"apiAccounts\">API account</a>'s individual IP list. You can specify a range, "
"an individual IP address, or an IP in CIDR notation. Compressed and "
"uncompressed IPv6 addresses are also permitted. Example: "
"<code>[\"1.1.1.1-1.1.1.8\", \"1.2.3.4\", \"1.5.5.0/24\"]</code>  The default "
"is [\"0.0.0.0/0\",\"::/0\"], which permits API calls from all IP addresses.  "
"For security, we strongly recommend specifying appropriate IP addresses in "
"your company. Child customers of a reseller can modify this setting to meet "
"their requirements.  API calls from forbidden IPs would get an HTTP 403 "
"response with a body <code>{\"code\" : \"AccessDenied\", \"message\" : "
"\"This request is rejected due to IP restriction.\"}</code>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/emailAddress/description
msgid "Email address of the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/patch/requestBody/description
msgid ""
"Specify the fields to be updated.  Omitted fields will be unchanged. "
"Settings within the <i>configs</i> field can only be set by a reseller on "
"behalf of a child customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/delete/summary
msgid "Delete a customer"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/delete/responses/204/description
msgid "The customer was deleted."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/delete/responses/404/description
msgid "The customer could not be found."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/delete/responses/409/description
msgid ""
"The customer could not be deleted because it is still configured with a "
"product. <a href=\"#operation/patch-ngadmin-customers-id\">Update the "
"customer</a> to remove the product before trying again."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers~1{id}/delete/description
msgid ""
"In the past, resellers could use this API to delete a child customer. This "
"API has been deprecated. A reseller can instead disable a child customer by "
"<a href=\"#operation/patch-ngadmin-customers-id\">updating the customer</"
"a>'s configuration to remove its products and modifying its status to "
"\"suspended\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/summary
msgid "Create a customer"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"The customer was successfully created. The response body will have details "
"including default values of settings not explicitly specified in the request "
"body including the API key. Resellers can give the API name and key to their "
"customer to allow them to manage their CDN use by calling APIs.\n"
"The Location header will also include a URL to the customer account. "
"Example: <code>Location: https://ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/ngadmin/customers/"
"12345678</code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customerId/description
msgid "ID of the new customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiKey/description
msgid "API key corresponding to the administrator API account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/responsiblePerson/description
msgid "Name of a person responsible for the customer account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/title
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/configs/title
msgid "customerConfigs"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/ipWhiteList/description
msgid ""
"List of IP addresses from which API calls using API accounts are permitted.  "
"You can specify a range, an individual IP address, or an IP in CIDR "
"notation.  Example: <code>[\"1.1.1.1-1.1.1.8\", \"1.2.3.4\", "
"\"1.5.5.0/24\"]</code>  The default is [\"0.0.0.0/0\"], which permits API "
"calls from all IP addresses. For security, we strongly recommend specifying "
"appropriate IP addresses for your company.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/content/application~1json/schema/properties/phone/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/phone/description
msgid "A phone number for the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL of the new customer. The URL follows this format: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/ngadmin/customers/{customerId} where {customerId} represents "
"the ID of the newly created customer. If you would like to get the customer "
"ID, simply extract the last portion of the path and ignore the rest. The ID "
"can be used to query or update the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/description
msgid ""
"Resellers can use this API to create a child customer. If the customer "
"requires deployment to PoPs in mainland China the reseller is responsible "
"for collecting and verifying the <i>phone</i>, <i>address</i>, "
"<i>responsiblePerson</i>, and <i>chinaBizInfo</i> fields for the customer "
"before enabling deployment to China."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/responsiblePerson/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/responsiblePerson/description
msgid "Name of a person responsible for the customer account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/ipWhiteList/description
msgid ""
"List of IP addresses from which API calls using API accounts are permitted. "
"This list works with each <a href=\"#operation/post-ngadmin-"
"apiAccounts\">API account</a>'s individual IP list.  You can specify a "
"range, an individual IP address, or an IP in CIDR notation. Compressed and "
"uncompressed IPv6 addresses are also permitted. Example: "
"<code>[\"1.1.1.1-1.1.1.8\", \"1.2.3.4\", \"1.5.5.0/24\"]</code>  The default "
"is [\"0.0.0.0/0\", \"::/0\"], which permits API calls from all IP addresses. "
"For security, we strongly recommend specifying appropriate IP addresses in "
"your company. Child customers of a reseller can modify this setting to meet "
"their requirements. API calls from forbidden IPs would get an HTTP 403 "
"response with a body <code>{\"code\" : \"AccessDenied\", \"message\" : "
"\"This request is rejected due to IP restriction.\"}</code>.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/post/requestBody/description
msgid "The request body describes the new customer account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/summary
msgid "Get list of customers"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/description
msgid "The response contains a list of customers."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/count/description
msgid "Number of customers."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/description
msgid "List of customers."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/description
msgid "Summarizes a single customer account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/customerId/description
msgid ""
"Customer ID. Pass it to the <a href=\"#operation/get-ngadmin-customers-"
"ID\">Get Customer Details API</a> to retrieve more information."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/parentId/description
msgid "ID of the parent customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/name/description
msgid "Name of the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/status/description
msgid "Account status."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/creationTime/description
msgid "RFC 3339 date indicating when the customer account was created."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/lastUpdateTime/description
msgid "RFC 3339 date indicating when the customer account was last updated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/type/description
msgid "Indicates the type of account."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/phone/description
msgid "Phone number of the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customers/items/properties/products/description
msgid "List of products that the customer has access to."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/responses/403/description
msgid "The API call is not permitted."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/description
msgid ""
"<b>Resellers</b> can use this API to get a list of their child customers. "
"Query parameters filter results.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"Maximum number of customers to return. The default is to return all "
"customers."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/2/description
msgid ""
"Keyword to search for in the customerId, apiName, name, and description "
"fields of customer accounts."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/3/description
msgid "Comma-separated list of IDs of customers to return."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/4/description
msgid "Return customers with particular status."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/5/description
msgid ""
"Comma-separated list of products which can include 'CDN' representing CDN "
"Pro and 'HDT' representing High-Speed Data Transmission'. Only customers "
"with access to the specified products will be returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/6/description
msgid ""
"This parameter is processed only when <i>products</i> is also specified. If "
"true, a customer is considered a match when a specified product is in either "
"the customer's <i>configs.products</i> or <i>configs.historicalProducts</i> "
"list. If false or omitted, only <i>configs.products</i> is checked."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/7/description
msgid "Sort accounts by their creation time or when they were last updated."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/8/description
msgid ""
"Order of customers returned by the API, either <i>asc</i> for ascending or "
"<i>desc</i> for descending."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1customers/get/parameters/9/description
msgid ""
"Comma-separated list of regional offices of customers to return. A case "
"insensitive search for the regional offices will be done.  You can specify a "
"value ending with an asterisk character, '*', in which case all customers "
"whose regional offices begin with the preceding characters will be returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/summary
msgid "Get client regions"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/responses/200/description
msgid ""
"The response body contains a list of regions. You can specify a region's "
"code in an edge hostname's client zone rule."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/items/properties/code/description
msgid "A code representing a region."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/items/properties/name/description
msgid "A description of the region.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/description
msgid ""
"Get a list of client regions that can be used in <a href=\"#operation/"
"createEdgeHostname\">edge hostname client zone rules</a>. Query parameters "
"allow you to filter and sort the results."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/parameters/0/description
msgid "Return regions whose code or name contains the specified value.\n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"Order of client regions returned. Use 'asc' for ascending order or 'desc' "
"for descending order."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1clientRegions/get/parameters/2/description
msgid ""
"Limit the returned regions to those where an ISP operates. The value should "
"be one of the ISP codes returned by the <a href=\"#operation/get-cdn-"
"isps\">ISPs API</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/summary
msgid "Get a list of API calls"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/description
msgid "The response body contains a summary of API calls that have been made."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/hasMore/description
msgid ""
"Indicates whether there are more API calls available beyond the current page "
"of results."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/description
msgid "A list of API calls."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/apiRequestId/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiRequestId/description
msgid "A unique ID representing the API call."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/requestTimestamp/description
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 date with UTC time that indicates when the API call was made. "
"Example: \"2020-04-24T20:09:15Z\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/requestURL/description
msgid "URL that was requested."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/requestMethod/description
msgid "Indicates the HTTP method that was used. Example:  \"GET\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/isSafe/description
#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/isSafe/description
msgid ""
"A value of <i>true</i> indicates the API call is read-only and does not "
"modify any resource. A value of <i>false</i> means a modification can "
"occur.  For example, a call to create or deploy a property is not safe, so "
"<i>false</i> would be returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/responseCode/description
msgid "HTTP response code for the API call."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/onBehalfOf/description
msgid ""
"A non-empty value indicates that an API call was made on your behalf. For "
"example, the CDN Pro support team may have helped you with configuration."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/apiCalls/items/properties/apiName/description
msgid ""
"Indicates the API account name used in the API call. This field will be "
"omitted if the admin API account is used."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/description
msgid "Echoes the query parameters used in the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/method/description
msgid "The HTTP method filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/path/description
msgid "The path filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/safe/description
msgid "The safe filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/caller/description
msgid "The API account name or ID filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/onbehalfof/description
msgid "The on-behalf-of filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/status/description
msgid "The HTTP response status code filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/startdate/description
msgid "The start of the time period filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/enddate/description
msgid "The end of the time period filter applied to the request."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/before/description
msgid ""
"The cursor ID used to retrieve API calls made before a specific API call."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filters/properties/limit/description
msgid "The maximum number of API calls to return."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/description
msgid ""
"Retrieve a list of recent API calls that have been made by you or on your "
"behalf. API calls triggered by portal users are included as well. Query "
"parameters allow you to filter results. By default, API calls made in the "
"last 24 hours will be returned if the startdate and enddate parameters are "
"unspecified."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/0/description
msgid "Filter results by HTTP method. Example: \"PATCH\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"Specify the path portion of a URI to filter out calls to a particular path. "
"For example, to get a list of calls to property API endpoints using https://"
"ngapi.{{siteDomain}}/cdn/properties, you would specify \"path=/cdn/"
"properties\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/2/description
msgid ""
"Filter results by whether they are considered safe or not. Safe calls do not "
"make changes to resources."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/3/description
msgid ""
"Filter results by specifying the API account name or API account ID. You can "
"get IDs by obtaining a <a href=\"#operation/get-ngadmin-apiAccounts\">list "
"of your API accounts</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/4/description
msgid ""
"The value can be a customer ID to return API calls made on behalf of that "
"customer, <i>none</i> to fetch API calls made directly or through the "
"portal, or <i>any</i> to fetch calls made on behalf of any customer. The "
"last option would apply only if you are a reseller."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/6/description
msgid ""
"Filter API calls by specifying a comma-separated list of HTTP response "
"status codes. You can also specify individual status codes such as \"200\" "
"or \"404\". You can also  pass \"2xx\", \"3xx\", \"4xx\", or \"5xx\" to "
"request all API calls whose response status codes begin with the first "
"digit. For example, \"2xx\" will include API calls whose status were "
"\"200\", \"201\", and \"204\"."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/7/description
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 format date indicating the beginning of the time period when API "
"calls were made. Example: <code>startdate=2019-10-30T00:00:00Z</code>. This "
"field should be specified along with the enddate parameter or left empty."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/8/description
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 date indicating the end of the time period when API calls were "
"made. Example: <code>enddate=2019-10-30T00:00:00Z</code>. This field should "
"be specified along with the startdate parameter or left empty."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/9/description
msgid ""
"Return API calls made before the API call with this ID. Use the "
"<code>apiRequestId</code> from a previous response to paginate through "
"results."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/10/description
msgid ""
"Maximum number of API calls to return. The default is to return up to 100 "
"calls."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls/get/parameters/11/description
msgid ""
"An optional header that resellers can use to specify whether to include data "
"from children customers. <table><tr><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th></"
"tr><tr><td>self-only</td><td>Include API calls of the caller.</td></"
"tr><tr><td>children-only</td><td>Include API calls of children customers "
"only.</td></tr><tr><td>self+children</td><td>Include API calls of both the "
"caller and children customers.</td></tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1{id}/parameters/0/description
msgid ""
