"response headers, and caller's IP address."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/summary
msgid "Count API calls"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/description
msgid ""
"Returns a count of API call records made by the calling customer. Supports "
"optional filtering by time window, request path prefix, and whether to "
"include calls made on behalf of the caller."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/parameters/0/description
msgid ""
"Start of the query time window, as an RFC 3339 UTC datetime (e.g. "
"`2019-03-01T10:00:00Z`). When omitted together with `enddate`, the window "
"defaults to the last 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/parameters/1/description
msgid ""
"End of the query time window, as an RFC 3339 UTC datetime (e.g. "
"`2019-03-31T10:00:00Z`). When omitted together with `startdate`, the window "
"defaults to the last 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/parameters/2/description
msgid ""
"Filter to API calls whose request path starts with this prefix. Case-"
"insensitive; normalized to lowercase with a leading `/`. Must start with one "
"of: `/cdn/`, `/ngadmin/`, `/hdt/`. A 400 error is returned for disallowed "
"prefixes."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/parameters/3/description
msgid ""
"Scope toggle. `true` — only count calls made directly by the calling "
"customer. `false` — also include calls made on behalf of the calling "
"customer. "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/description
msgid ""
"A named data series containing the count of matching API calls. Currently "
"returns a single data point timestamped at `startdate`."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/title
msgid "DataSeries"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/description
msgid "A named, unit-tagged data series."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataName/description
msgid "Human-readable name of the data series."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataUnit/description
msgid "Unit of measurement for `data` values."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataSeries/items/title
msgid "DataPoint"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataSeries/items/description
msgid "A single data point with a timestamp and a numeric value."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataSeries/items/properties/timestamp/description
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 UTC timestamp. For the counts endpoint this is always the "
"`startdate` (start of the query window)."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dataSeries/items/properties/data/description
msgid "The count of API calls matching the query."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1ngadmin~1apicalls~1counts/get/responses/400/description
msgid ""
"Bad Request — invalid date format, invalid path prefix, or missing/invalid "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/summary
msgid "Get system configuration"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/description
msgid "The response contains the system configuration."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/baseDirectives/description
msgid "A list of Edge Logic directives that are available to everyone."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/advancedDirectives/description
msgid ""
"A list of advanced Edge Logic directives that can be enabled by contacting "
"our support team."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/description
msgid "Describes the price for traffic and requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perGB/description
msgid ""
"Describes the price for each gigabyte of traffic used  within each server "
"group."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perGB/properties/standard/description
msgid ""
"Price in US dollars per gigabyte of traffic using the standard server group."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perGB/properties/premium/description
msgid ""
"Price in US dollars per gigabyte of traffic using the premium server group."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perGB/properties/deluxe/description
msgid ""
"Price in US dollars per gigabyte of traffic using the deluxe server group, "
"formerly referred to as \"premium+\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perGB/properties/ultra/description
msgid ""
"Price in US dollars per gigabyte of traffic using the ultra server group."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/publishedPrice/properties/perMHttpsReq/description
msgid "Price in US dollars of one million HTTPS requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/description
msgid ""
"This field lists nonstandard ports that can be used to handle HTTP and HTTPS "
"requests. If your website uses a nonstandard port which is not listed, "
"please contact our support team. You can specify one of these port numbers "
"in the <i>extraServicePorts</i> field of your property configuration."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/http/description
msgid ""
"Specifies ports other than the default 80 which can be used to handle HTTP "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/extraServicePorts/properties/https/description
msgid ""
"Specify ports other than the default 443 which can be used to handle HTTPS "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/advancedFeaures/description
msgid ""
"List of advanced features that can be enabled for customers via the service "
"quota API. \"realTimeLog\" is an advanced feature allowing a customer to "
"monitor requests from visitors to the content as they are received. "
"\"nearChina\" is an advanced feature allowing use of a special server group "
"to provide better performance to visitors in China for domains without ICP "
"Beian. \"originShield\" allows use of an extra layer of servers in front of "
"a property's origin servers. Please contact our support team if you require "
"an advanced feature."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/oldestPropertyValidationTime/description
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 date indicating the oldest validated property that can be deployed. "
"Properties validated before this date must be re-validated before you can "
"deploy them. Example: \"2021-02-05T00:00:00Z\""
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/baseLbDirectives/description
msgid ""
"List of Edge Logic directives that can be used in the <i>loadBalancerLogic</"
"i> field of a property by everyone."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/advancedLbDirectives/description
msgid ""
"A list of advanced Edge Logic directives that can be enabled for use in the "
"<i>loadBalancerLogic</i> field of a property. If you require one that is not "
"enabled for your account, please contact our support team."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/supportedLanguages/description
msgid ""
"Indicates the languages that a customer can specify as preferred for "
"notifications.\n"
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Value</th><th>Language</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>en</td><td>English</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>cn</td><td>Chinese</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>jp</td><td>Japanese</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td>kr</td><td>Korean</td></tr>\n"
"</table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1systemConfigs/get/description
msgid ""
"This API returns system configuration settings including supported [Edge "
"Logic directives](</docs/edge-logic/supported-directives>), advanced Edge "
"Logic directives, the default pricing for traffic, and nonstandard ports "
"that can handle HTTP and HTTPS requests. Please note that your account may "
"not have access to the advanced Edge Logic directives or features. Please "
"contact our support team if you require access to a particular directive, "
"feature, or port that is not listed."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/summary
msgid "Create a service quota for a customer"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"The service quota was successfully created. A Location header will contain a "
"URL to the newly created service quota."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL to the new service quota. The URL follows this format: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn/serviceQuotas/{serviceQuotaId} where {serviceQuotaId} "
"represents the ID of the newly created service quota. If you would like to "
"get the service quota ID, simply extract the last portion of the path and "
"ignore the rest. The ID can be used to query, update, or delete the service "
"quota."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/description
msgid ""
"A reseller can use this API to define CDN Pro service quotas for a child "
"customer. The child customer cannot have quota levels greater than those of "
"the reseller. "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/customerId/description
msgid "ID of the customer for which to create the service quota."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/status/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/status/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/status/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Indicates the status of the customer's access to the CDN Pro product.  An "
"<i>active</i> customer has full access. A <i>suspended</i> customer no "
"longer has access but may return to use the service. A <i>trial</i> customer "
"is one with trial settings which may be more limited than those of a "
"customer with the <i>active</i> status. A <i>terminated</i> customer no "
"longer has access."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/contractId/description
msgid "ID representing the contract, used for billing."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accountManagerEmail/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accountManagerEmail/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/accountManagerEmail/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid "An email address representing the account manager."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/trialDeadline/description
msgid ""
"A date in RFC 3339 format indicating when the trial expires. This field is "
"required if the <i>status</i> field's value is <i>trial</i>. "
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/usageLimitDays/description
msgid ""
"This setting applies to trial customers. It is used to limit traffic use. It "
"represents the number of days over which the traffic amount designated by "
"the <i>usageLimitDollar</i> field can be used. For example, a value of 90 "
"for <i>usageLimitDays</i> and 50 for <i>usageLimitDollar</i> means the "
"customer can use up to $50 worth of total traffic over a 90 day period. A "
"value of 0 means there is no limit on the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/usageLimitDollar/description
msgid ""
"This setting applies to trial customers. It represents the amount of traffic "
"valued in US dollars that is permitted to be used over a period of time  set "
"by the <i>usageLimitDays</i> field. For example, a value of 90 for "
"<i>usageLimitDays</i> and 50 for <i>usageLimitDollar</i> means the customer "
"can use up to $50 worth of total traffic over a 90 day period. The dollar "
"value is based on CDN Pro's default pricing. A value of 0 means there is no "
"limit on the customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowDeploymentInChina/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowDeploymentInChina/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1customer~1{customerId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowDeploymentInChina/description
msgid ""
"Indicates whether deployment to PoPs in mainland China is permitted. An ICP "
"Beian license is required for web content to be hosted on servers within "
"China. A reseller must collect and verify a child customer's name, address, "
"phone, responsible person, and China business information before enabling "
"deployment to China. Those settings are specified when <a href=\"#operation/"
"post-ngadmin-customers\">creating</a> or <a href=\"#operation/patch-ngadmin-"
"customers-id\">updating</a> a customer."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/hostnameLimit/description
msgid "Maximum number of hostnames allowed in production."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/edgeHostnameLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/edgeHostnameLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/edgeHostnameLimit/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid "Maximum number of edge hostnames that can be created."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum number of file purges allowed in the staging environment in a 24-"
"hour rolling window."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInStaging/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum number of directory purges allowed in the staging environment in a "
"24-hour rolling window. This limit is also used as the maximum number of "
"regular expression purges allowed in staging."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/filePurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum number of file purges allowed in the production environment in a 24-"
"hour rolling window."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/dirPurgeQuotaInProduction/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum number of directory purges allowed in the production environment in "
"a 24-hour rolling window. This limit is also used as the maximum number of "
"regular expression purges allowed in production."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/prefetchQuota/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/prefetchQuota/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/prefetchQuota/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid "Maximum number of prefetch requests in a 24-hour window."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/propertyLimit/description
msgid "Maximum number of properties that can be created."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/certificateLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/certificateLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/certificateLimit/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid "Maximum number of certificates that can be created."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/logConfigLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/logConfigLimit/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/logConfigLimit/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid "Maximum number of log configurations."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedCacheDirectives/description
msgid ""
"A list of advanced [Edge Logic directives](</docs/edge-logic/supported-"
"directives>) that are permitted to be used in addition to standard ones."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/serviceQuotaList/items/properties/allowProduction/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowProduction/description
#. (+4 more)
msgid ""
"Indicates if deployment to production servers is permitted. Deployment to "
"staging servers is always permitted."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/advancedFeatures/description
msgid ""
"List of advanced features available to the customer.\n"
"Available features can be found in the response of the <a href=\"#operation/"
"get-cdn-systemConfigs\">system configuration API</a>. Currently supported "
"features include: \"realTimeLog\", which allows a customer to monitor "
"requests from their client as they occur; \"nearChina\" allowing a customer "
"without ICP Beian to use a server group consisting of nodes close to "
"mainland China; and \"originShield\", which provides an extra layer of "
"servers between the CDN Pro edge servers and origin servers. Please contact "
"our support team if you require an advanced feature."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/title
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/title
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/title
#. (+3 more)
msgid "directiveParameterLimits"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Contains limits on values of Edge Logic directives. These override the "
"default maximums."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/properties/maxLimitRate/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/properties/maxLimitRate/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1serviceQuotas~1{serviceQuotaId}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/directiveParameterLimits/properties/maxLimitRate/description
#. (+3 more)
msgid ""
"Maximum number of bytes per second that can permitted in the [limit_rate](</"
"docs/edge-logic/supported-directives#limit_rate>) directive."
