msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedOperations/properties/logConfigs/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedOperations/properties/logConfigs/description
msgid ""
"Whether the API account can access the <a href=\"#tag/Log-Configuration-"
"Management\">log configuration</a> (/cdn/logConfigs) endpoints. The value "
"'read' can be given to an operator API account to restrict it to getting the "
"list of log configurations or a log configuration's details."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/description
msgid ""
"List of IDs of resources that can be accessed. This works with "
"<i>allowedOperations</i>. For example, suppose "
"allowedOperations.certificates is set to <i>true</i>. If "
"allowedResources.certificates is not specified, then all certificates are "
"accessible. However, if allowedResources.certificates is specified, then "
"access is restricted to the listed certificates. If the list is empty, no "
"certificates are accessible."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/certificates/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/certificates/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/certificates/description
msgid "IDs of certificates that can be accessed."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/properties/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/properties/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/properties/description
msgid ""
"IDs of properties that can be accessed. If you specify property IDs in this "
"field, property management endpoints are limited to the accessible "
"properties. In addition, because hostnames are specified in property "
"definitions, any restrictions on properties also limit the hostnames that "
"are accessible through other API endpoints including reports, log "
"configuration management, hostnames, and content management. For example, "
"calls to the <a href=\"#tag/Hostnames\">hostnames</a> (/cdn/hostnames) "
"endpoints will return information about hostnames only if they belong to the "
"list of allowed properties. Similarly, the <a href=\"#tag/Reports\">reports</"
"a> (/cdn/report) endpoints will return data only for hostnames belonging to "
"the allowed properties."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/edgeHostnames/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/edgeHostnames/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1apiPermissions~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/allowedResources/properties/edgeHostnames/description
msgid "Edge hostnames that can be accessed."
msgstr ""

