#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/groups/items/properties/group/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1bandwidthSummary/post/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/groups/items/properties/group/description
#. (+5 more)
msgid ""
"Name of a group.  \"\\_\\_all\\_\\_\" is a special group encompassing all "
"groups."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/post/description
msgid ""
"Get a summary of requests during a time period. You can filter and group "
"results by hostnames, server groups, property IDs, or property hostnames. If "
"you are a reseller, you can also filter and group by customerIds to "
"distinguish your child customers' requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/post/parameters/1/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/get/parameters/2/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1bandwidthSummary/post/parameters/2/description
#. (+2 more)
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 date indicating the end of the time period. The time must be "
"specified using the UTC timezone; it cannot be an offset. Example: "
"<code>enddate=2019-11-14T00:00:00Z</code> Your enddate may be rounded up to "
"the nearest minute, hour, or day depending on the <i>type</i> parameter. For "
"example, if you enter <code>enddate=2019-09-05T03:14:01Z&type=hourly</code>, "
"the response includes data ending 2019-09-05T04:00:00Z. Due to latency "
"associated with new traffic data, enddate should be no later than five "
"minutes before the current time. This ensures you get the most accurate "
"results."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/post/parameters/2/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/get/parameters/3/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1edgeStatusSummary/post/parameters/2/description
#. (+5 more)
msgid ""
"Limit the results to the specified scheme. By default, data from HTTPS and "
"HTTP requests is returned."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/get/description
msgid ""
"Get a summary of requests during a time period. Query parameters let you "
"specify the time period, scheme, and whether to group the results. If you "
"are a reseller, you can also group by customerIds to distinguish your child "
"customers' requests."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1reqSummary/get/parameters/4/description
msgid ""
"You can group results using any combination of up to two of 'hostnames', "
"'serverGroups', 'customerIds', 'propertyHostnames',  'propertyIds', and "
"'legacyTypes' by specifying a comma-separated list of the keywords."
msgstr ""

