"An optional header that resellers can use to specify whether to include data "
"from children customers. <table><tr><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th></"
"tr><tr><td>self-only</td><td>Return webhooks of the caller only.</td></"
"tr><tr><td>children-only</td><td>Include webhooks of children customers only."
"</td></tr><tr><td>self+children</td><td>Include webhooks of both the caller "
"and children customers.</td></tr></table>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/summary
msgid "Create a webhook"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"The webhook was successfully created. A Location header containing the URL "
"of the new webhook is returned. Example: <code>Location: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn/webhooks/60a2e69806d5583a81ad9500</code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL to the new webhook. The URL follows this format: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn/webhooks/{webhookId} where {webhookId} represents the ID "
"of the webhook. If you would like to get the webhook ID, simply extract the "
"last portion of the path and ignore the rest. You can use the ID to create, "
"update, or delete the webhook."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/description
msgid ""
"Create a webhook. It can be used to notify you when an asynchronous task "
"completes. You can reference a webhook when <a href=\"#operation/"
"createDeployment\">creating a deployment task</a>, <a href=\"#operation/"
"createPurge\">creating a purge request</a>, <a href=\"#operation/post-cdn-"
"prefetches\">creating a prefetch request</a>, or <a href=\"#operation/"
"createValidationTask\">creating a validation task</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/description/description
msgid "Optional description of the webhook."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/url/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/url/description
msgid ""
"That URL that will be called when the asynchronous task has completed. The "
"HTTP POST method will be used. The body will in JSON format:\n"
"<code>\n"
"{ \"subject\": \"{some text}\",\n"
"  \"taskType\": \"{task type}\",\n"
"  \"taskList\": [\n"
"    { \"taskId\": \"{task id 1}\",\n"
"      ...\n"
"    },\n"
"    { \"taskId\": \"{task id 2}\",\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
"</code>"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/credentials/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks~1{id}/get/responses/200/content/application~1json/schema/properties/credentials/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks~1{id}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/credentials/description
msgid ""
"Optional credentials passed to the URL. If requiring credentials your server "
"should support HTTP Basic authentication the same way we do. Refer to <a "
"href=\"#section/Authentication\">Authentication summary</a>. In particular, "
"the <i>password</i> will be the secretKey encoded with the current date."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1webhooks/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/credentials/properties/user/description
