#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/summary
msgid "Create a secret"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/responses/201/description
msgid ""
"The secret was successfully created. A Location header containing the URL of "
"the new secret is returned. Example: <code>Location: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn/secrets/60d6707cca3e387d2a28fc9e</code>. \n"
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/responses/201/headers/Location/description
msgid ""
"URL of the new secret. The URL follows this format: https://ngapi."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn/secrets/{secretId} where {secretId} represents the ID of "
"the newly created secret. If you would like to get the secret ID, simply "
"extract the last portion of the path and ignore the rest. The ID can be used "
"to query, update, or delete the secret."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/responses/409/description
msgid "A secret with this name already exists."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/description
msgid ""
"Create a secret to protect sensitive text from being exposed in a property's "
"Edge Logic or origins. Refer to the secret in your property's Edge Logic "
"using the <code>$SECRET(secretName)</code> syntax. You can also set "
"<code>origins.authentication.awsS3.secretKey</code> to "
"<code>$SECRET(secretName)</code>. When you deploy the property, references "
"to <code>$SECRET(secretName)</code> will be replaced by the text."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/name/description
msgid ""
"The name of the secret. It can consist of letters, numbers, hyphens, "
"underscores, and periods. Refer to this in your Edge Logic using the "
"<code>$SECRET(secretName)</code> syntax, or use it as the value of "
"<code>origins.authentication.awsS3.secretKey</code>."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/description/description
#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets~1{secretID}/patch/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/description/description
msgid ""
"A description of the secret. This may be useful for recording the purpose of "
"the secret."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/requestBody/content/application~1json/schema/properties/secret/description
msgid ""
"The sensitive text you want to protect. When you deploy your property, "
"references to <code>$SECRET(secretName)</code> in your Edge Logic or in "
"<code>origins.authentication.awsS3.secretKey</code> will be replaced by this "
"text. The secret can consist of printable ASCII characters along with the "
"tab, newline, and return characters."
msgstr ""

#. /paths/~1cdn~1secrets/post/requestBody/description
msgid ""
"The request body contains the name of the secret along with the sensitive "
"text to protect."
msgstr ""

