#. /paths/~1cdn~1report~1logDownload/post/description
msgid ""
"Get access logs representing requests to one or more hostnames in your "
"deployed properties. These logs contain data from requests made 2 or more "
"hours earlier. By default, only logs within the past 14 days are available, "
"and they are separated into files each covering part of a day.\n"
"\n"
"To obtain logs for a hostname, you must first specify the format of the logs "
"by <a href=\"#operation/post-cdn-report-logConfigs\">creating a log "
"configuration</a> that applies to the hostname. Requests to your content "
"made after the applicable log configuration has been created will be logged. "
"Otherwise, no logs will be available for download.\n"
"\n"
"For example, suppose you define a log configuration format as follows:\n"
"<br/>\n"
"<pre>\n"
"%cltip %rmtuser [%utctime] \"%method %url %protocol\" %statuscode %rspsize "
"\"%referer\" \"%ua\" %rsptime\n"
"</pre>\n"
"\n"
"This API will return a list of available logs such as:\n"
"\n"
"<pre>\n"
"{\n"
"  \"logs\":[\n"
"          {\n"
"          \"dateFrom\":\"2024-03-21T00:00:00Z\",\n"
"          \"dateTo\":\"2024-03-21T00:29:59Z\",\n"
"          \"fileSize\":105878,          \"logUrl\":\"https://"
"logdcenter.chinanetcenter.com/logd/v2/download/"
"0621c8fc87ba5d548ab0a878ff6f077351d082ecdf60cbd6d60e98?"
"traceId=ac6d696c657765625f74657374cf0000018e604202d8cd1e39\",\n"
"          \"hostname\":\"mydomain.domain.info\"\n"
"          }\n"
"        ]\n"
"}\n"
"</pre>\n"
"\n"
"The logUrl field contains a URL to a gzip-compressed log file consisting of "
"rows such as the following:<br/>\n"
"<pre>\n"
"9.8.7.6 - [21/Mar/2024:19:59:57 +0000] \"GET http://mydomain.domain.info/i/"
"js/tab.js HTTP/1.1\" 304 529 \"http://mydomain.domain.info/?q=downloads\" "
"\"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like "
"Gecko) Chrome/95.0.4638.54 Safari/537.36\" 76\n"
"</pre>\n"
"\n"
"The URL is valid for 24 hours. If you need to download the logs again after "
"that, you must make another request to this API to get a new URL.\n"
msgstr ""

