#. /components/securitySchemes/API Key/description
msgid ""
"All requests to the CDN Pro platform must be authenticated using an API "
"account name and key assigned to your organization. For security, the API "
"key is not passed directly but is secured as described in the example script "
"below.\n"
"\n"
"The authentication type is HTTP Basic, and the authorization string is "
"specified in the HTTP header field called Authorization.\n"
"\n"
"<pre>\n"
"<code>\n"
"#!/bin/bash\n"
"#URL of the CDN Pro API server\n"
"API_SERVER=https://ngapi.{{siteDomain}}\n"
"\n"
"#You will be given the following information by the {{title}} sales team\n"
"USER=\"{API user name}\"\n"
"API_KEY=\"{API key (make sure to escape the $ sign if any)}\"\n"
"\n"
"#Date in RFC 1123 format\n"
"DATE=`LC_TIME=\"C\" date -u \"+%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%S GMT\"`\n"
"\n"
"#Generate the password. Raw output from openssl by adding the \"-binary\" "
"flag\n"
"passw=$(echo -n \"$DATE\" | openssl dgst -sha1 -hmac \"$API_KEY\" -binary | "
"base64)\n"
"echo \" \"\n"
"\n"
"#Construct the curl command to query list of properties\n"
"apiCall=\"curl -i --url '${API_SERVER}/cdn/properties'\n"
"               -X GET\n"
"               -u $USER:$passw\n"
"               -H 'Date: $DATE'\n"
"               -H 'Accept: application/json'\"\n"
"\n"
"eval $apiCall\n"
"echo \" \"\n"
"</code>\n"
"</pre>\n"
"\n"
"If you are a reseller you can also specify a child customer's ID in an On-"
"Behalf-Of HTTP header field to make API calls to manage your child "
"customer.\n"
"\n"
"A more advanced Bash script allowing you to make calls to many CDN Pro APIs "
"is available <a href=\"https://github.com/mileweb/CDNProCLI/tree/master/cdn/"
"bash\">here</a>."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/0/description
msgid ""
"If your content requires TLS, you must create a certificate and <a "
"href=\"#tag/Deployment-Management\">deploy</a> it along with associated <a "
"href=\"#tag/Property-Management\">properties</a>.  For test purposes, you "
"can create a self-signed certificate. Certificates are versioned. Each "
"update to a certificate generates a new immutable version. You can choose to "
"deploy any version to staging or production. If your property's origin "
"requires authentication using a certificate, you should also call the API to "
"create the required certificate, upload it, and deploy to use it. If you are "
"a reseller, you may share your certificates with your child customers who "
"can then use the certificates, but not modify them."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/1/description
msgid ""
"A property is the configuration of one or more hostnames (domains) that need "
"to be <a href=\"#tag/Deployment-Management\">deployed</a> to the CDN Pro "
"servers. A property can have multiple versions. A property version that has "
"been deployed cannot be updated or <a href=\"#tag/Property-"
"Validation\">validated</a> again. You can <a href=\"#operation/"
"createPropertyVersion\">create a new version of a property</a> by making a "
"clone (or copy) of an existing version. <p>The following figure shows the "
"steps for creating an acceleration service for a hostname.</p><img src=\"/"
"static/content-assets/mileweb/docs-content-cdn/en/docs/resources/images/"
"getting-started-flowchart.png\">"
msgstr ""

#. /tags/2/description
msgid ""
"After you <a href=\"#operation/createProperty\">create a property</a>, you "
"must validate it to ensure that the settings are syntactically correct "
"before you can <a href=\"#tag/Deployment-Management\">deploy</a> it to "
"staging or production. The validation process is an asynchronous action. "
"APIs are available to check the status of your validation tasks."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/3/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to define secrets that are used to hide sensitive "
"information, such as preventing a password from being visible in an API call "
"or within the CDN Pro portal. For example, a secret could be a key used to "
"authenticate client requests to your origin server. By creating a secret and "
"referring to it in your [Edge Logic](</docs/edge-logic/intro>) using the "
"secret's name via the syntax `$SECRET(secretName)`, or by setting "
"`origins.authentication.awsS3.secretKey` to `$SECRET(secretName)`, the key "
"itself would not be exposed when viewing a property through the CDN Pro "
"portal or fetching it using the CDN Pro API."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/4/description
msgid ""
"Deployment is the process of pushing out your property and certificate "
"configurations to the CDN Pro cache servers. We highly recommend you [deploy "
"to our <i>staging</i> environment to test your configurations before "
"deploying to <i>production</i>](</docs/portal/edge-configurations/testing-"
"property>). <h2>Testing a property deployed to production</h2> After you <a "
"href=\"#operation/createEdgeHostname\">create an edge hostname</a> and set "
"your DNS server to point the edge hostname to your property's hostname, you "
"can browse your content under the hostname."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/5/description
msgid ""
"You must <a href=\"#operation/createProperty\">create properties</a> to "
"manage your configurations on CDN Pro. Several APIs are available that allow "
"you to get summarized information about the hostnames (or domains) of "
"properties that have been <a href=\"#operation/createDeployment\">deployed</"
"a> to production or staging."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/6/description
msgid ""
"You must create an edge hostname for properties deployed to production. You "
"can define rules to apply to visitors from different client zones that are "
"combinations of geographic regions and ISPs.  You must modify your DNS "
"records to point each property's hostnames to an edge hostname in order for "
"visitor requests to be handled by CDN Pro. Different properties' hostnames "
"may point to the same edge hostname if the same rules apply."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/7/description
msgid ""
"Call our report APIs to get information about your visitors including edge "
"and origin traffic, requests, status code details, and log files."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/8/description
msgid ""
"Add text annotations to highlight events related to traffic to your "
"hostnames. These annotations will appear in the [CDN Pro portal](https://"
"console.{{siteDomain}}/cdn) when you look at the reports."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/9/description
msgid ""
"The content management APIs allow you to request an update (or purge) of "
"your cached content ahead of the schedule determined by your <a "
"href=\"#operation/getPropertyVersion\">property configuration</a>.  You can "
"purge files or directories.  The purge requests are asynchronous. APIs are "
"available for you to check the status of your purge requests. You can also "
"prefetch URLs to warm up your cache in advance of requests from visitors. "
"This allows you to manage traffic to your origin servers."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/10/description
msgid ""
"Create and manage users who access the [CDN Pro portal](https://console."
"{{siteDomain}}/cdn)."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/11/description
msgid ""
"Create and manage additional API accounts used to call the CDN Pro APIs. You "
"can customize which set of endpoints the API accounts can access by "
"specifying <a href=\"#operation/post-cdn-apiPermissions\">API permissions</"
"a>."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/12/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to update customer-level portal settings and contact "
"information as well as to reset the administrator API key. Resellers can "
"also create, update, delete, and get a list of customer accounts."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/13/description
msgid ""
"Obtain a summary of API calls that have been made by you or on your behalf."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/14/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to fetch CDN settings that apply to your account. If "
"you are a reseller, you can use APIs to manage the service quotas of your "
"child customers."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/15/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to customize what a <a href=\"#operation/post-ngadmin-"
"apiAccounts\">CDN Pro API account</a> can do by specifying the categories of "
"accessible endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/16/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to define webhooks or callbacks that are invoked when "
"an asynchronous operation such as a deployment, purge, or prefetch request "
"completes."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/17/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to customize the format of the access logs you can "
"download using <a href=\"#operation/get-cdn-report-logDownload\">our API</"
"a>. Logs are available for a hostname only for requests that are made after "
"you have defined an applicable log configuration format for the hostname."
msgstr ""

#. /tags/18/description
msgid ""
"These APIs allow you to create log aggregation points which are ingestion "
"URLs that receive raw log entries from the CDN Pro servers. This option is "
"available for those who use our realTimeLog advanced feature."
msgstr ""

